      "writtenOn": "2023-02-28T23:41:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These RMI failures will also occur occasionally during a normal successful resume. There\u0027s a race condition in the resume path. We could try to avoid this by adding a delay after resume, but that will complicate this code a bit. Since missing a single temp reading isn\u0027t critical, I prefer keeping it simple.\n\nSo IMO the error message needs to be reworded to be less definitive, or we could switch to a fail counter. The first failure would print the generic RMI failure message. After at least 2 consecutive failures, we could print the more definitive message like:\n\"RMI: The AP is failing to respond despite being powered on. The AP is probably hung.\"",
      "revId": "cf8d98899c277016152829abccba6c12e645f7c7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
