      "message": "Done.\n\nI\u0027ve also updated `MKBP` since that also results in log spam. With both changes, we now get:\n\n```\n23-03-01 13:57:33.063 [134.439000 RMI: Unexpected command value in out bound message]\n23-03-01 13:57:33.428 [134.675600 MKBP not cleared within threshold, toggling.]\n23-03-01 13:57:33.667 [135.449900 RMI: Unexpected command value in out bound message]\n23-03-01 13:57:34.449 [135.678100 MKBP: The AP is failing to respond despite being powered on. The AP is probably hung.]\n23-03-01 13:57:34.682 [136.459300 RMI: The AP is failing to respond despite being powered on. The AP is probably hung.]\n```\n\nIt\u0027s still a bit of duplication, but (IMO) much cleaner than it was.",
